<html>
    <head>
        <title>About | NYC Bird Orchestra</title>
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css">
    </head>
    <body>
        <header>
            <div class="container header-content">
                {% include "nav.njk" %}
            </div>
        </header>

        <main class="container">
            <section class="about-intro">
                <h1>About NYC Bird Orchestra</h1>
                <p>A collective musical composition made from the birds we notice across New York City.<br>Each sighting is a small contribution to a shared citywide score.</p>
            </section>

            <hr>

            <section class="about-community">
                <h2>Five boroughs. One community.</h2>
                <p>From a familiar robin in a park to a new species on your block, every observation belongs here. NYC Bird Orchestra brings neighbors together through birdwatching, shared curiosity, and sound. You do not need to be a musician or an expert birder. Start with a bird you recognize and help build a composition that reflects the city around us.</p>
            </section>

            <hr>

            <section class="about-steps">
                <h2>How It Works</h2>
                <div class="steps">
                    <article>
                        <h3>1. Spot</h3>
                        <p>Notice a bird in your neighborhood. Remember its species, borough, and the time you saw it.</p>
                    </article>
                    <article>
                        <h3>2. Submit</h3>
                        <p>Add your sighting using the short form. Include an observation if you would like to share more.</p>
                    </article>
                    <article>
                        <h3>3. Observe</h3>
                        <p>Return to the orchestra to explore the score. Your bird joins sightings from across the city.</p>
                    </article>
                </div>
            </section>

            <hr>

            <section class="about-score">
                <h2>Understanding the Score</h2>
                {# <p>Read the score from left to right. Each bird marker represents a sighting.</p>
                <div class="score-example-placeholder">An example sighting on the score will appear here.</div>
                <p>Borough determines the vertical position. Each borough has its own line.</p>
                <p>Time determines the horizontal position. Earlier sightings appear toward the left.</p>
                <p>The marker shows the bird species. Select it to read the observation.</p> #}
                <img src="/assets/instruction.png" width=100%>
            </section>

            <hr>

            <section class="about-invitation">
                <h2>Join the Orchestra</h2>
                <p>Your next bird sighting could be the next note. Add a bird to become part of the city's composition.</p>
                <a class="button" href="/form">Add a Bird</a>
            </section>
        </main>

        <footer>
            <div class="container">
                <p>NYC Bird Orchestra</p>
                <p>A community composition, one sighting at a time.</p>
            </div>
        </footer>
        <script src="/script.js" defer></script>
    </body>
</html>
